{{Quote|Whistling birds are a powerful defense against multiple enemies. Use them sparingly, for they are rare.|The Armorer|<ref name="Chapter 3" />}}
A '''whistling bird''' was a type of weapon used by [[Mandalorian]]s. They were small guided munitions placed in [[Mandalorian vambrace]]s which, when deployed, flew through the air while making a whistling noise before striking the target and [[Death|killing]] them with a small explosion.<ref name="Chapter 3" />

==History==
[[File:WhistlingBirds-SWL98.png|thumb|left|250px|Din Djarin launches whistling birds while rescuing Grogu.]]
In [[9 ABY]],<ref name="Date">{{MandoDate|3}}</ref> a Mandalorian known as "[[the Armorer]]" made whistling birds for the Mandalorian [[bounty hunter]] [[Din Djarin]]. He subsequently used whistling birds to kill four [[stormtrooper]]s simultaneously during a [[Incident on Nevarro|mission]] to rescue [[Din Grogu|Grogu]] on [[Nevarro]].<ref name="Chapter 3" /> He later used several whistling birds during a [[Bothan-Five incident|scuffle]] with the [[Devaronian]] [[mercenary]] [[Burg]], but failed to land a single projectile due to the close confines of the room.<ref name="Chapter 6">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 6: The Prisoner}}</ref> In [[35 ABY]],<ref name="Date-35">{{FilmDate|IX|Diss's appearance}}</ref> the bounty hunter [[Carib Diss]] wore a [[Mandalorian]] [[Mandalorian vambrace|rocket gauntlet]] equipped with whistling birds while residing on [[Kijimi]].<ref name="TROS VD">''[[Star Wars: The Rise of Skywalker: The Visual Dictionary]]''</ref>

{{Weapon-stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
[[File:Whistling-Birds-Concept.png|thumb|250px|Concept art of Din Djarin using whistling birds.]]
Whistling birds first appeared in [[Chapter 3: The Sin|Chapter 3]] of [[Jon Favreau]]'s [[2019]] [[Disney+]] television series ''[[Star Wars: The Mandalorian]]'',<ref name="Chapter 3" /> which aired on [[November 22]], 2019.<ref name="DTCI">{{WebCite|url=https://lumiere-a.akamaihd.net/v1/documents/the_mandalorian_project_one-sheet_10_ec1e005f.pdf|text=The Mandalorian Media Kit|work=[https://dtcimedia.disney.com Disney Direct-to-Consumer & International]|archivedate=20230315011507}}</ref>

